  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we subtract and add $7$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-1}{4x-7}=\\frac{4x-7+7-1}{4x-7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-7+7-1}{4x-7} & =\\frac{4x-7}{4x-7}+\\frac{7-1}{4x-7} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{6}{4x-7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=1$ and $b=6,$ and we get\n\n$$\na+b=1+6=7.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
